  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reinforcing law enforcement and community engagement systems for the enhanced protection of the Northern White-cheeked Crested Gibbon in the Nam Et - Phou Louey NPA core Zone, Lao PDR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to conserve globally significant populations of Northern White-cheeked Crested Gibbon (Nomascus leucogenys) in the Nam Et-Phou Louey NPA by enabling concentrated enforcement interventions in strategic areas of the NPA Core Zone with gibbon populations. The following objectives and associated activities will be carried out: (1) Strengthen forest-based patrolling in and around gibbon areas, by (a) strengthening and equipping five foot patrol sectors, one rapid response team and three community-based law enforcement networks (CLEANs) nearest to the high-risk areas for gibbons in the NEPL NPA, and (b) Increase the patrolling effort in and near gibbon territories; (2) Improve cooperation between agencies and stakeholders responsible for protecting gibbons and their habitat, by (a) conducting meetings between NEPL NPA management, District Office of Natural Resources and Environment (DONRE) and village clusters in key areas to assess the progress of the CLEAN initiative, discussing ways to expand the mechanisms being piloted in targeted CLEAN communities, and planning the next stages of implementation with the goals of professionalizing law enforcement, and (b) supporting foot patrol team leaders and CLEAN representatives to attend the monthly strategic planning meetings to create adaptive, strategic plans for protecting gibbons and to report on findings from CLEANs and patrols in areas with highest gibbon abundance.</narrative>
  </description>
